Point at the new public R2 URL, and document deployment

The bucket moved to a new public address, so R2_PUBLIC_URL is updated in the
Worker config and the local env.

DEPLOY.md covers the parts that are easy to get wrong:

- The three secrets, what each does, and that SESSION_SECRET is generated
  rather than looked up. They are deliberately absent from the repository.
- Deploying from a machine, and from a connected GitHub repository. The
  Worker name has to match the name in wrangler.jsonc or the build fails,
  and the root directory is the repository root.
- What to check after the first deploy: collection status until pending
  reaches zero, then the self-test, which proves the search works against
  real photos rather than leaving "no match" ambiguous.
- Why local development is slow and production is not, so performance is
  never judged from the wrong environment.
- That the bucket being public means direct r2.dev URLs bypass the session
  check the app applies to /media paths.

